<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shaanxi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shaanxi is a province of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> valley, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi'an</a>. The Wei valley, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a>, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Zhou and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and the seat of the Western Zhou, Qin, Western Han and Tang capitals. The north of the province, on the Loess Plateau, was the base of the Chinese Communists at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yanan">Yan'an</a> from 1935 to 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shaanxi.jpg" alt="Shaanxi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (Cat's diary) 猫猫的日记本 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qianling_Mausoleum_25_2013-08.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
